    <name>Notices &amp; Releases</name>
    <intro>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Types%20of%20Communication%20-%20Notices%20%20Releases.png" alt="" width="1575" height="300"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" style="float: left; padding-right: 10px;" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Notices%20%20Releases.png" alt="" width="100" height="100"&gt;Information about public notices and releases, including types of media and audiences.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;</intro>
    <introformat>1</introformat>
    <content>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Types%20of%20Communication%20-%20Notices%20%20Releases.png" alt="" width="1575" height="300"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;The Maine DOE communicates with various audiences, including school administrators and staff and media outlets. Some modes of communication and sharing information are reserved for specific audiences. It is important to understand our different methods of communication to determine the appropriate one to use. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of these communication types are available in the &lt;a href="https://somdoegeneralproduction.crm9.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid=baad3b2b-d201-4316-9e19-af1ea100f6b5&amp;amp;pagetype=entitylist&amp;amp;etn=comm_newsroomrequest&amp;amp;viewid=a9c34696-d0a9-44c3-aa2c-7383fbad60c9&amp;amp;viewType=1039" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Communications Workflow.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Priority Notice&lt;/strong&gt; - A priority notice is a targeted communication to a specific audience. It is not intended for the general public. Priority notices are sent through Mailchimp and are not posted publicly. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Current priority notice audiences: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Assistant / Superintendents &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;span style="mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Assistant / Principals &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Education Organizations &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Business Managers &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;span style="mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Curriculum Coordinators &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;CTE Directors &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"&gt;Technology Directors &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"&gt;Special Education Directors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"&gt;School Counselors/Social Workers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"&gt;School Nurses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media Advisory&lt;/strong&gt; - Media advisories are sent only to the media to invite them to a specific event hosted by the Maine DOE. Events worth promoting may be inaugural, celebratory, or unique in nature, where you would want news outlets to cover a story. &lt;a href="http://Media releases share announcements and important Maine DOE news with the press and our larger audience. These are often issued after an event has happened to inform the public. They are also used to share information about ongoing/upcoming initiatives and programs. Please use this template for additional guidance. If you would like your media release to be shared on the Maine DOE Newsroom, please contact the Director of Communications." target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Please use this template for additional guidance&lt;/a&gt;. Media advisories are not posted to the Maine DOE Newsroom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media Release&lt;/strong&gt; - Media releases share announcements and important Maine DOE news with the press and our larger audience. These are often issued after an event has happened to inform the public. They also share information about ongoing/upcoming initiatives and programs. &lt;a href="http://Media releases share announcements and important Maine DOE news with the press and our larger audience. These are often issued after an event has happened to inform the public. They are also used to share information about ongoing/upcoming initiatives and programs. Please use this template for additional guidance. If you would like your media release to be shared on the Maine DOE Newsroom, please contact the Director of Communications." target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Please use this template for additional guidance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a&gt;.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportAnnotations]--&gt; If you would like your media release to be shared on the Maine DOE Newsroom, please contact the Director of Communications. &lt;/p&gt;</content>
